dsToNumber(text)`.\n       - Implemented deterministic subtotal and grand total word override.\n     - `utils/privacyMasker.js`:\n       - Added `addressWords` filtering for PAN, bank, account, and state/cities.\n       - Added deterministic subtotal calculation.\n     - `utils/aiExtractor.js`:\n       - Updated `GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION` with string schema, numeric instructions, and line item boundary rules.\n   - **In Progress / Pending in Server:**\n     - `server.py`: In `analyze_bill`, add the direct check right after `sanitize_and_clean_invoice(parsed)`:\n       ```python\n       subtot = float(cleaned.get(\"subtotal\") or 0.0)\n       dec_tot = float(cleaned.get(\"declared_total\") or 0.0)\n       cgst = float(cleaned.get(\"cgst\") or 0.0)\n       sgst = float(cleaned.get(\"sgst\") or 0.0)\n       igst = float(cleaned.get(\"igst\") or 0.0)\n       if subtot > 0 and dec_tot < (subtot * 0.5):\n           cleaned[\"declared_total\"] = round(subtot + cgst + sgst + igst, 2)\n           cleaned[\"total_declared\"] = cleaned[\"declared_total\"]\n       ```\n     - `utils/aiExtractor.js`: Ensure `extractInvoiceFromDocument` also applies this fallback directly if client-side fallback is executed.\n     - Restart daemon task for `server.py 3000` and verify with end-to-end Python test.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - The root cause of the \"774\" extraction is that on the scanned invoice, \"774\" appears as an HSN fragment, partial tax row, or serial number. Gemini was latching onto it as `declared_total` because it was near the bottom before the word description.\n   - Enforcing `if declared_total < (subtotal * 0.5)` catches any misread where `declared_total` is smaller than half of the subtotal (e.g. 774 vs 3805) and deterministically substitutes `subtotal + taxes` (3805 + 684.90 = 4490) or the parsed words (`FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY` = 4490).\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - *Error:* `AssertionError` in python test because `server.py` had not yet implemented